                 [--voice-barge-in] [--responsive]
                 [--audio-file AUDIO_FILE | --text TEXT | --text-mode | --hands-free]

Production voice loop with optional development input injection.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --latency-trace-dir LATENCY_TRACE_DIR
                        Opt-in content-free timing reports in a dedicated
                        bounded directory.
  --barge-in            Opt-in keyboard cancellation: Enter/s stops; n then
                        Enter captures a new request.
  --voice-barge-in      Experimental concurrent wake monitoring with speaker-
                        reference rejection; implies --barge-in.
  --responsive          Release a complete short first sentence to Piper
                        before model EOF; later packing stays unchanged.
  --audio-file AUDIO_FILE
                        Run once using an audio file instead of microphone
                        capture.
  --text TEXT           Run once using text, bypassing capture, normalization
                        and STT.
  --text-mode           Interactively enter text while retaining the
                        conversation.
  --hands-free          Continuously wait for the offline wake word, then
                        retain a bounded microphone request (requires enabled
                        wake word and ALSA).
